" ============================================================================
" ~/.vimrc -- loader
" ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
" The configuration itself lives in ~/.vim/vimrc.d/, one file per area. Files are
" sourced in numeric order, which matters:
"
"   00-plugins.vim            vim-plug block -- the plugin list (must be first)
"   10-options.vim            core :set options, autoread, resize behaviour
"   20-mappings.vim           mapleader, editing/motion maps, OSC 52 clipboard
"   30-plugin-config.vim      per-plugin settings: fzf, floaterm, bookmarks, ...
"   40-colorscheme.vim        theme selection + per-theme highlight overrides
"   50-coc.vim                coc, gd, peek-definition popup, signify signs
"   60-coc-semantic.vim       theme-adaptive semantic-token highlighting
"   70-sessions-startify.vim  vim-obsession sessions, startify
"
" Why the order is load-bearing: plugins must be registered before anything
" configures them; mapleader must be set before the mappings that use it; the
" colourscheme and its per-theme overrides must be in place before 50-/60-, whose
" resolvers read what the theme actually defines.
"
" To add a section, drop in a new numbered file -- no change needed here. Renumber
" rather than reorder, since sourcing follows the sorted filename.
"
" Gotcha: script-local (s:) names are file-scoped, so an s: function and everything
" that calls it -- including <SID> mappings -- must live in the same file.
"
" `:source $MYVIMRC` still re-reads everything.
" ============================================================================

for s:file in sort(glob('~/.vim/vimrc.d/*.vim', 0, 1))
  execute 'source' fnameescape(s:file)
endfor
